\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Evaluation utility and expected performance}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{Let #{u(q,\tau)\in\mathbb R} be the utility assigned by the independent
evaluator to a completed evaluation trajectory. For policy #{\pi}, inference
protocol #{D}, and budget #{b}, define expected performance}

##{
  J_{\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}}}(\pi;D,b)
  =\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal Q_{\mathrm{ev}},\,
    \tau\sim\mathbb P^{D,b}_{q,\pi}}[u(q,\tau)].
}

\p{Expected utility is the standard policy-evaluation object in reinforcement
learning; see \citet{Section 3.5}{sutton2018reinforcement}. The FTIP specialization makes
the inference protocol and budget visible.}

\p{A success probability is obtained by taking #{u} to be a binary indicator.
Scores with different units should not be combined without a declared
normalization or multi-objective order.}
